Subject: [PATCH] feat: translate only the experiences an actual proposal
 selects
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per feedback: the site_copy/backfill approach eagerly translates the
whole catalog, burning Lara quota on experiences no proposal has ever
selected. Landing + configurator (site_copy) stay eager since that's
fixed, small UI text — but experience content (title/description,
sections, facts) is per-experience marketing copy that should only be
translated for what a given proposal actually shows.

- translateExperience.ts: syncFullExperienceTranslations(experienceId)
  re-fetches an experience's content + all its sections/facts and syncs
  all three via the existing per-row sync functions (no duplicated
  logic).
- New /api/translate-proposal-experiences route: given a leadId, reruns
  the same generateProposal() matching used by the results page to find
  the featured experience + suggested add-ons, then translates only
  those.
- craft-your-experience/page.tsx: fires this request (fire-and-forget,
  same pattern as notify-new-proposal) right after a proposal is saved,
  so translation happens in the background at generation time instead
  of via a manual bulk backfill.

The one-time catalog backfill script stays in the repo as an optional
tool, but this makes it unnecessary for normal operation going forward.

